- `sys.parse(declaration)` reads `sys.argv()`; `sys.parse(declaration, arguments)` reads an explicit list of texts.
- Returns a record containing one field per declared flag plus `arguments` (list), `help` (yes/no), and `usage` (text).
- Flag declaration: list of records with `name`, `type` (`text`, `number`, `yes/no`/`boolean`, `path`), optional `takes_value`, `default`, `required`, `help`.
- Reserved names: `arguments`, `help`, `usage`. Reject unknown declaration fields, duplicate names, required+default, and `takes_value: no` on non-boolean.
- Parsing supports `--flag value`, `--flag=value`, repeated flag last-wins, flags after positionals, empty text value, `--` terminator, `--help`/`-h`.
